From: squadai-stable <noreply@local>
Date: 2026-06-27
Subject: [PATCH] aorus17 (0035) -- quiet the RM-level [CLOSE] path diag (NV_DBG_INFO)

Observability/noise fix, follow-up to aorus16 (0034). 0034 rate-limited the three
heavy dumpers and demoted the UVM-side "AORUS UVM [CLOSE]" one-liner to pr_debug,
but it did NOT touch the RM-level per-site [CLOSE] marker emitted by
tb_egpu_lever_m_close_path_diag() in kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c.

Measured in vivo 2026-06-27: a CUDA process exit fires this marker 4x per close
(close-entry / pre-stop / post-shutdown / close-exit); across several processes a
single session logged ~312 of these lines. They are pure close-path telemetry for
the (now-complete) Problem 2/4 diagnosis, not real-time errors.

Fix -- pure logging level change, nothing else:
  - Demote the per-site [CLOSE] marker from NV_DBG_ERRORS to NV_DBG_INFO so it is
    silent at the default debug level but still available when NVreg debug is
    raised (and keeps the NVRM device prefix, unlike pr_debug). Matches the file's
    own convention for non-error diagnostics (lines ~1004/1125/1436 etc.).

NOT changed: the R4 gate (os_pci_is_egpu_target, line ~1378) still confines this
to the eGPU; the is_last_close full dump still fires (and is rate-limited by 0034);
the M-recover state machine is untouched. Pure dmesg-volume throttle.
---
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
index 0e1f319..caac9cc 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-lever-m-recover.c
@@ -1380,7 +1380,7 @@ void tb_egpu_lever_m_close_path_diag(nv_linux_state_t *nvl,
 
     nv = NV_STATE_PTR(nvl);
 
-    NV_DEV_PRINTF(NV_DBG_ERRORS, nv,
+    NV_DEV_PRINTF(NV_DBG_INFO, nv,
         "AORUS Lever M-recover [CLOSE]: site=%-15s usage_count=%ld%s\n",
         site, usage_count, is_last_close ? " (LAST-CLOSE)" : "");
 
